  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the top small-business government contractors by contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Total obligations to the firms shown equal $20.3B. The leaders span supply, logistics, technology, and specialized services, with one firm receiving $2.5B in obligations and several others receiving between $916M and $608M. The list is partial because the fiscal year is not complete. Readers should treat the totals as current, fiscal year to date contract obligations rather than full-year results. The ten firms shown represent the largest obligated totals among small businesses in this period, and together they account for a substantial share of small-business contracting activity through the reported date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who tops the list of small-business contractors by obligations?",
        "body": "ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. tops the list with $2.5B in obligations. The next largest obligations are $916M and $900M, held by AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC and GENERAL MATTER, INC. respectively. The top ten firms range from $2.5B down to $608M in obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How much do the top small businesses account for in total obligations?",
        "body": "The page reports total obligations of $20.3B for the period. The ten listed firms together include obligations of $2.5B, $916M, $900M, $835M, $794M, $710M, $685M, $674M, $641M, and $608M. These figures are fiscal year to date and represent the largest small-business obligation totals recorded so far in FY2026."
      }
    ]
  },
